{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_expressbackend", "label": "ExpressBackend", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pick it for the middleware ecosystem or an incremental migration, not for perceived simplicity \u2014 Fastify is faster and both are equally simple from an actor-ts perspective."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_expressbackendoptions", "label": "ExpressBackendOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_maxbodybytes", "label": "withMaxBodyBytes (1 MiB default)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_withapp", "label": "withApp (bring-your-own Express app)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "actor-ts registers its routes on the same app, so existing routes and middleware keep working without swapping the whole HTTP stack; it is also the only way to set trust proxy or wrap the app in node:https for TLS."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_trust_proxy_antipattern", "label": "app.set('trust proxy', true) is not the safe setting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "true compiles to a trust-everything function, so proxy-addr never truncates the list and req.ip becomes the leftmost X-Forwarded-For entry \u2014 exactly the value the client sent. Every common proxy appends, so there is no deployment in which true is correct; a numeric hop count is address-blind and believes the header on a request that passed no proxy at all."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_middleware_ecosystem", "label": "Express middleware wraps actor-ts routes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_ws_handshake_through_app", "label": "WebSocket handshakes go through app.use", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A websocket() route is registered as an ordinary GET, so a middleware that answers cancels the handshake and onClientConnected never fires. Two caveats: one that neither answers nor calls next() leaves the client waiting, and a rejection body only reaches the client on runtimes that allow writing to a hijacked upgrade socket \u2014 Bun and Node do, Deno does not."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_tls", "label": "Express TLS via node:https", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_performance", "label": "Express throughput (40K-60K req/sec)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Express middleware chain has more overhead than Fastify hooks; P50 latency is similar and throughput is what differs."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_trust_proxy_antipattern", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_fastify_trustproxy_true_antipattern", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_expressbackend", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_expressbackendoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_expressbackendoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_maxbodybytes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_expressbackendoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_withapp", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_withapp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_trust_proxy_antipattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/backends/express.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_withapp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_backends_express_tls", "relation": "references", "confidence"